      "content": "okay i see the logs now. the data shows the package was handled perfectly—no drops, no impact alerts, and the internal temp was stable the whole time. the sensor data basically suggests the damage didn't happen during transit. \n\ngiven that we know it likely wasn't the carrier's fault, what's your recommendation for the refund? we need to be careful about how we handle this so we don't just hand out money to people for things they might have broken themselves, but i also don't want a massive escalation on our dashboard.",
